From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: amami: give the cpus their rail and run them up to 1.5GHz

The Krait OPP table stops at 960MHz because nothing described VDD_APC,
so no rate could be checked against the voltage it needs.

VDD_APC is pm8841 s5, leading s6-s8, on SID 5. Its voltage register
reads 0xb4, 900mV (the same decode gives pm8941 s2 2.15V, which its
regulator reports). That is stock's CORE_VOLTAGE_BOOTUP, and all four
cores' ACCs show BHS on with the LDO bypassed and powered down, so the
cores run straight off it. The L2 SAW already holds stock's
all-phases value (0x10003 at +0x1c).

Describe s5 as vdd_apc, fixed at 900mV since nothing can drive it
through the SAW yet, and make it the cpus' supply. Give the OPPs the
voltages of every bin in Sony's stock device tree, plus a plain
opp-microvolt at the highest of them for a bin stock has no table for:
with a supply set, a unit whose bin had no voltages would lose the whole
table. The OPP core disables any rate the rail cannot give, so each unit
runs as far as 900mV covers for its bin: this one (speed2-pvs4-v0) to
1497.6MHz at 895mV, the slowest bin to 883.2MHz. All of it lives in
amami's dts: the shared table keeps its 960MHz cap for boards that
describe no rail.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-amami.dts
@@ -68,6 +68,477 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	cpu-supply = <&vdd_apc>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	cpu-supply = <&vdd_apc>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	cpu-supply = <&vdd_apc>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	cpu-supply = <&vdd_apc>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * Voltages are the qcom,speedN-pvsM-bin-v0 tables of Sony's stock device
+ * tree, every bin, so the table holds on any unit: qcom-cpufreq-nvmem picks
+ * the one the fuses name (this one's is speed2-pvs4-v0), and the plain
+ * opp-microvolt, the highest any bin needs at each rate, covers a bin
+ * stock has no table for. Each is the least the cores need at that rate:
+ * stock runs them in BHS mode, straight off VDD_APC, at these voltages.
+ * vdd_apc is fixed at 900mV, and the OPP core drops every rate whose
+ * voltage it does not cover: this unit runs to 1497.6MHz (895mV), the
+ * slowest bin to 883.2MHz. The rest, up to 2150.4MHz at 1V on this unit,
+ * comes with control of the rail.
+ */
